RUNG 4 — contains: a filter for the lines that mean "found inside"
  The first rung that knows a marker: <CONTAINS>, the root. A line means "contains" when
  the root reaches it: walking down from each file's text, through lines whose right end
  appears inside their left. Everything else is an association.

  usage:  4-contains FILE.eoe ... | 2-show          what contains what
          4-contains --rest FILE.eoe ...            everything else: words, tower, sources

contains lines:
    waiting = every text the root <CONTAINS> points at
    while waiting:
        whole = take one from waiting
        for each line leaving whole:
            if line.right is text inside whole:
                mark line as contains
                add line.right to waiting

main:
    if --rest:  write every line not marked
    else:       write the marked lines, plus the root's own lines
                (so reading the output again finds the same contains)
